<title>USA: Reebok sued TriStar over product placement - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Reebok sued TriStar over product placement - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reebok International Ltd sued Sony's TriStar Pictures, accusing the studio of breaking a product-placement pact for the movie &quot;Jerry Maguire,&quot; The Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>Reebok says it provided more than $1.5 million for the film so that audiences would remember an uplifting Reebok commercial that was supposed to be part of the film's ending, the WSJ said.</p>
<p>The dispute over the alleged deletion of the Reebok advertisement is at the heart of the suit filed in U.S. District Court in Los Angeles by Reebok, seeking $120 million in damages, the report said.</p>
</text>
